    "type": "question",
    "label": "5",
    "prompt": "If the letters of the word GUMTREE and the letters of the word KOALA are combined and arranged into a single twelve-letter word, in how many of these arrangements do the letters of KOALA appear in their correct order, but not necessarily together?",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$1\\,995\\,840$",
      "worked": "Choose five positions for K, O, A, L, A, in that order: $\\binom{12}{5}$ choices. Arrange the seven letters of GUMTREE in the remaining positions, accounting for the two identical Es.\n$$\\begin{aligned}N&=\\binom{12}{5}\\times\\frac{7!}{2!}\\\\&=792\\times2520\\\\&=1\\,995\\,840.\\end{aligned}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
